iteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8d10a60022bdfd06","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Calibration command section","norm_id":"n0d9a4188869b5ac4","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor tries to run the calibration snippet but the plan does not contain the runnable body."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Point the calibration verify step at a concrete artifact path (e.g. redstart-calibrate.py) with the full script committed alongside redstart-proof.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Drive divergent fold points through a path that actually consults snapshot_alpha (e.g. `rebar compact-all` with `[compact] snapshot_alpha` set in each clone's rebar.toml and threshold high enough that only the byte arm selects), because the single-ticket `rebar compact <id> --threshold=9999` never reads snapshot_alpha and will skip on the `preflock <= threshold` gate, folding nothing.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Single-ticket `compact_cli` reads only threshold/horizon: `_cfg = config.compose_config(...).compact; threshold = _cfg.threshold; horizon = _cfg.COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS` (src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:98-100) — no snapshot_alpha.","Gate at compact.py:151-153: `if preflock <= threshold: ... 'below threshold ({preflock} <= {threshold}) — skipping compaction'; return 0` — with --threshold=9999 a few comments always skip.","`snapshot_alpha` is threaded ONLY through `compact_all_cli`/`_scan_snapshot_state` (compact.py:549,567) and the close trigger (compact_trigger.py:110,124); grep of src/rebar/_commands confirms no alpha reference in the single-ticket path or `_compact_locked`.","needs_folding's adaptive-recurrence arm (compact_plan.py:243-247) is the only place alpha matters, and it is unreachable from `rebar compact <id>`."],"finding":"The proof's fold-point mechanism cannot exercise the byte-alpha arm: `rebar compact <ticket> --threshold=9999` never reads snapshot_alpha and skips on the plain `preflock <= threshold` gate, so both clones fold nothing and the proof 'converges' vacuously — proving nothing about ADR 0118's divergent byte-cost folds.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2e9529eb4b1978c1","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Proof command, steps 5-6 ('add four large A-tail comments and compact with --threshold=9999 --horizon=0, so the byte alpha arm (not count) creates one fold point')","norm_id":"n0c024892250dfd22","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running redstart-proof.py: each clone's `rebar compact <ticket> --threshold=9999` prints 'below threshold — skipping compaction', writes no new SNAPSHOT, so no divergent fold points exist; the final `rebar show` comparison passes trivially and the script exits 0.","equitable-upper-hammerkop later enables snapshot_alpha in reliance on a green gate that never tested the byte arm."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace steps 5-6's `rebar compact <ticket> --threshold=9999 --horizon=0` with `rebar compact-all --horizon=0` (or the store-wide sweep) after setting `[compact] snapshot_alpha` and `threshold` in the clone's rebar.toml so the byte arm — not the count arm — selects the ticket; add an assertion that a new SNAPSHOT file was actually written in each clone before the fetch/merge/replay/fsck comparison, so a skipped-no-op fold fails the proof loudly rather than passing as spurious convergence.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a proving command that affirmatively asserts absence, e.g. `grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*snapshot_alpha' rebar.toml && exit 1 || true`, in addition to `git diff --exit-code`.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4687,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: \"`compact.snapshot_alpha` remains absent from th